  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "loongport",
      "text": "`loongport` is a [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness)\n(DSH) Cordis bundle for verified LoongPort OpenAI-compatible providers. It also includes an\nadvanced CLI for custom endpoints."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install in DeepSeek Harness",
      "text": "Install the public package into the DSH profile you use:\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile <profile> add loongport\n```\n\nOpen **Settings → LoongPort** in DSH, then:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install in DeepSeek Harness",
      "text": "1. Select a verified provider. The default is DeepSeek's official API at\n   `https://api.deepseek.com/v1`; BestAPI (`https://api.bestapi.store/v1`) is the\n   verified relay option.\n2. If you need an account, use the provider's **Register** or **Sign in** link. It opens the\n   provider's own website in your browser.\n3. Generate an API key with the provider and paste it into the dialog.\n4. Select `deepseek-v4-flash` or `deepseek-v4-pro`, then save."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install in DeepSeek Harness",
      "text": "The signed LoongPort directory is the authority for provider identity, URLs, available models,\nand any published invitation code. VeriDrop data, when shown, is only a display-only health\nobservation and cannot change provider configuration. DSH credentials store API keys; the\nSettings page only retains whether a key is configured."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install in DeepSeek Harness",
      "text": "Version 0.2.0 does not automate browser authorization, collect browser sessions, or access\ncookies/local storage. Registration/login and API-key creation remain on the provider's site."
    },
    {
      "section": "Advanced custom endpoint",
      "text": "For a manually supplied OpenAI-compatible endpoint, run the CLI directly:\n\n```bash\nLOONGPORT_API_KEY='your-api-key' npx loongport dsh setup \\\n  --base-url https://relay.example.com/v1 \\\n  --model model-id \\\n  --write\n\nThe API key is read only from `LOONGPORT_API_KEY`; never place it in a command argument. You\ncan repeat `--model` to register more than one model."
    },
    {
      "section": "Advanced custom endpoint",
      "text": "By default, the command performs a dry run. Add `--write` to update DSH's\nconfiguration. It uses `$DSH_HOME` when set, otherwise `~/.dsh`, and writes:\n\n- `settings.yaml`: one selected `llm-pi-ai.providers.<route>` entry\n- `.credentials.yaml`: the selected credential name and API key (owner-only)\n\nOther DSH settings, provider routes, and credentials are preserved. The\ncommand uses DSH's built-in `llm-pi-ai` transport; it does not implement its\nown streaming, retries, or tool calls."
    },
    {
      "section": "Options",
      "text": "```text\n--base-url <url>              OpenAI-compatible HTTP(S) endpoint (required)\n--model <id>                  Model to expose; repeat for multiple models (required)\n--route <name>                DSH provider route (default: loongport)\n--credential-name <name>      DSH credential key (default: LOONGPORT_API_KEY)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Options",
      "text": "The CLI remains an explicit advanced path. It supports manually provisioned\nOpenAI-compatible endpoints, but does not automate third-party browser login, relay discovery,\ndesktop-app bridging, or automatic tier switching."
    },
    {
      "section": "Maintainers",
      "text": "Agents and maintainers should read the [agent guide](docs/maintainers/agent-guide.md)\nbefore changing the package and follow the [release runbook](docs/maintainers/releasing.md)\nbefore publishing."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "[MIT](LICENSE)"
    }
